{"id":"H0453","lemma":"אֱלִיהוּ","transliteration":"elihu","sayIt":"e-li-HU","language":"Hebrew","partOfSpeech":"","gloss":"Elihu","meaning":"A man of the tribe of Levi living at the time of United Monarchy, first mentioned at 1Sa.1.1;\nson of: Tohu (H8459);\nfather of: Jeroham (H3395); also called Eliab at 1Ch.6.27; Eliel at 1Ch.6.34;\n§ Elihu = \"He is my God\"\n1) the younger man who rebuked Job and his three friends\n2) an Ephraimite, Samuel's great grandfather\n3) a Manassite warrior chief for David\n4) son of Shemaiah and Korhite gatekeeper\n5) David's brother","glosses":["elihu","now elihu","when he","so elihu","then elihu"],"count":11,"occurrences":[{"chapterId":"1sa-1","v":1,"renderings":{"bsb":"of Elihu","kjv":"of Elihu"}},{"chapterId":"1ch-12","v":20,"renderings":{"bsb":"Elihu","kjv":"and Elihu"}},{"chapterId":"1ch-26","v":7,"renderings":{"bsb":"Elihu","kjv":"Elihu"}},{"chapterId":"1ch-27","v":18,"renderings":{"bsb":"was Elihu","kjv":"Elihu"}},{"chapterId":"job-32","v":2,"renderings":{"bsb":"of Elihu","kjv":"of Elihu"}},{"chapterId":"job-32","v":4,"renderings":{"bsb":"Now Elihu","kjv":"Now Elihu"}},{"chapterId":"job-32","v":5,"renderings":{"bsb":"But when he","kjv":"When Elihu"}},{"chapterId":"job-32","v":6,"renderings":{"bsb":"So Elihu","kjv":"And Elihu"}},{"chapterId":"job-34","v":1,"renderings":{"bsb":"Then Elihu","kjv":"Furthermore Elihu"}},{"chapterId":"job-35","v":1,"renderings":{"bsb":"And Elihu","kjv":"Elihu"}},{"chapterId":"job-36","v":1,"renderings":{"bsb":"And Elihu","kjv":"Elihu"}}],"elsewhere":[{"ref":"1 Samuel 1:1","note":"Now there was a certain man of Ramathaim Zophim, of the hill country of Ephraim, and his name was Elkanah, the son of Jeroham, the son of Elihu, the son of…","source":"web"},{"ref":"1 Chronicles 12:20","note":"As he went to Ziklag, some from Manasseh joined him: Adnah, Jozabad, Jediael, Michael, Jozabad, Elihu, and Zillethai, captains of thousands who were of…","source":"web"},{"ref":"Job 32:2","note":"Then the wrath of Elihu the son of Barachel, the Buzite, of the family of Ram, was kindled against Job. His wrath was kindled because he justified himself…","source":"web"}],"related":[{"id":"H0446","lemma":"אֱלִיאָב","transliteration":"eliav","gloss":"Eliab"},{"id":"H0026","lemma":"אֲבִיגַ֫יִל, אֲבִיגַ֫ל","transliteration":"avigayil","gloss":"Abigail"},{"id":"H0041","lemma":"אֲבִינָדָב","transliteration":"avinadav","gloss":"Abinadab"},{"id":"H0443","lemma":"אֶלְזָבָד","transliteration":"elzavad","gloss":"Elzabad"},{"id":"H8459","lemma":"תֹּחוּ","transliteration":"tochu","gloss":"Tohu"},{"id":"H3395","lemma":"יְרֹחָם","transliteration":"yerocham","gloss":"Jeroham"},{"id":"H8098","lemma":"שְׁמַעְיָ֫הוּ","transliteration":"shemayah","gloss":"Shemaiah"},{"id":"H6273","lemma":"עׇתְנִי","transliteration":"otni","gloss":"Othni"}],"senses":[{"id":"H0453H","gloss":"Elihu","relation":"H0453H ="},{"id":"H0453I","gloss":"Elihu","relation":"H0453I ="},{"id":"H0453J","gloss":"Elihu","relation":"H0453J ="},{"id":"H0453K","gloss":"Elihu","relation":"H0453K ="}],"sources":["STEPBible TBESH/TBESG lexicon (CC BY 4.0)","STEPBible TAHOT/TAGNT tagged text (CC BY 4.0)"]}